<title>CANADA: Canada census shows livestock output shifts west.</title>
<headline>Canada census shows livestock output shifts west.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beef and hog production continued to shift westward in the past decade, Statistics Canada's 1996 farm census data showed Wednesday.</p>
<p>The census was taken on May 14, 1996 and results were released exactly one year later.</p>
<p>			 1996	1991	1986</p>
<p>Beef Cows</p>
<p>Canada   Total  4,680,585  3,828,630 3,242,041</p>
<p>East Cnd Number   745,255    640,691   561,902</p>
<p>	   PCT	 15.9 pct   16.7 pct  17.3 pct</p>
<p>West Cnd Number 3,935,330  3,187,939 2,680,139</p>
<p>	   PCT	 84.1 pct   83.3 pct  82.7 pct</p>
<p>Hogs</p>
<p>Canada   Total 11,040,462 10,216,083 9,756,569</p>
<p>East Cnd Number 6,602,104  6,166,273 6,414,797</p>
<p>	   PCT	 59.8 pct   60.4 pct  65.7 pct</p>
<p>West Cnd Number 4,438,358  4,049,810 3,341,772</p>
<p>	   PCT	 40.2 pct   39.6 pct  34.3 pct</p>
<p>((Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
